<!--
  Imported into any project that references the GeometryEngine package.

  It carries the licences, and only the licences.

  The native binaries need nothing from here. They ship in the conventional
  runtimes/win-x64/native/ layout, the SDK copies that layout into the consumer's output on
  its own, and ManifoldNative's resolver probes it - so the native kernel engages without
  help. Copying them flat as well was tried and reverted: it worked, but it put a second
  3.2 MB copy of manifold.dll in every consumer's output for no benefit.

  The licences are the genuine gap. Package folders outside lib/ and runtimes/ are not
  copied anywhere, so without this the texts would sit in the NuGet cache and reach nobody.
  That matters because whoever builds on this library redistributes Manifold, oneTBB and ITT
  Notify inside their own output: Apache-2.0 clause 4(a) and BSD-3-Clause clause 2 bind them
  in their own right, and they can only discharge that if the texts are actually present to
  pass on.
-->
<Project>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../licenses/*.txt"
          Link="%(FileName)%(Extension)"
          CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest"
          Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
